        "Content": "Drumfad, Raphoe, Co Donegal F93 T263 \r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 28th of October 2026\r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nSuperb Location\r\n\r\nLocation Raphoe 4km, Lifford 7km, Letterkenny 17km, Ballybofey 23km. \r\n\r\nThe property is located off the N14, accessed from the R264, 4km east of Raphoe town. Population (2022) 1,161. Raphoe is a small town in Co Donegal in the north-west of Ulster. It is the main town in the fertile district of East Donegal known as the Laggan. The design of the modern town is traced to the Ulster Plantation of the early 17th century, who laid out the town with the 'Diamond' at its centre. Raphoe has 2 secondary and 2 primary schools, restaurants & Cafes, shops, pubs, a large hardware store, a mart, and sporting clubs. Letterkenny town is within reasonable driving distance where further amenities and transport links can be found. \r\n\r\nDescription Folio DL61153F\r\n\r\nThe subject property comprises of a 2-story detached dwelling house believed to date from the 1982. The c. 336 sq. m c. 3,616 sq. ft accommodation is current split into two houses. The single-story accommodation comprises of a kitchen, sitting room, dining room, four bedrooms and a family bathroom. The two-story accommodation comprises of a kitchen, sitting room, four bedrooms and three ensuite bathrooms. There is ample parking to the front and a side lawned garden. Access is via a long avenue from the N14. Excellent views of the verdant Donegal countryside. \r\n\r\nBER D2 # 119151025\r\n\r\nViewing - By appointment \r\n\r\nSolicitor David Lynch, Joynt & Crawford, 8 Anglesea St, Temple Bar, Dublin 2\r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
      },
